   "county": "Wabash",
   "jurisdiction": "Wabash County (unincorporated + Towns of LaFontaine, Lagro, Roann upon their adoption)",
   "action_type": "proposed",
   "instrument": "Plan Commission-initiated draft ordinance: 'AN ORDINANCE IMPOSING A TEMPORARY MORATORIUM ON THE ISSUANCE OF IMPROVEMENT LOCATION PERMITS FOR THE DEVELOPMENT OF DATA CENTERS' (ordinance number and adoption date blank; PDF watermarked 'DRAFT - Not Yet Approved'); duration: until the Zoning Ordinance is amended to regulate data centers or 18 months from adoption, whichever occurs sooner",
   "posture_source_words": "temporary moratorium on the acceptance, processing, and approval of all applications and permits ... for any structure related to a data center project, in all zoning districts",
   "observed_date": "2026-05-07",
   "date_note": "Official-source timeline: 2026-04-02 PC minutes — moratorium request discussed and TABLED 7-0 (motion Hann/Rice) to consider combining with BESS; 2026-05-07 PC minutes — 'Mr. Rice made a motion to approve the moratorium proposal and schedule a public hearing' — carried 8-0; 2026-07-02 PC minutes — 'the data center moratorium draft ordinance is expected to be placed on the Commission's August agenda for a public hearing', and BESS will be regulated separately (BESS already touched by the Commercial Solar Energy ordinance). NOT adopted as of latest posted minutes (2026-07-02); after the public hearing it must be certified to the Board of Commissioners (Tyler Niccum chairman, Cheryl Ross, Jeff D. Dawes) for final approval per I.C. 36-7-4-604/605. No expiry exists yet — 18-month clock starts only at adoption.",
   "effective_from": null,
   "effective_to": null,
   "verbatim_snippet": "There is now imposed a temporary moratorium on the acceptance, processing, and/or approval of all applications and permits, including the issuance of improvement locations permits, for any structure related to a data center project, including any construction or operation of data centers and all appurtenant facilities, in all zoning districts in the unincorporated areas of Wabash County. ... This Ordinance shall remain in effect until the Zoning Ordinance is amended to provide regulations related to data center projects within Wabash County, or for a period of eighteen (18) months from the date of adoption, whichever occurs sooner. [DRAFT - Not Yet Approved]",
   "url": "https://www.in.gov/counties/wabash/files/ordinances/Proposed-Data-Center-Moratorium.pdf",
   "doc_type": "ordinance PDF",
   "evidence_grade": "VERIFIED_AT_OFFICIAL_SOURCE",
   "why_codified_misses_it": "The county's own draft states the Zoning Ordinance (No. 2022-85-14) 'currently fails to provide any regulations related to data center projects' — the entire action lives in a draft PDF and plan-commission minutes on in.gov, with nothing in the codified text; a parallel data-center regulatory ordinance is also being drafted (per 2026-04-02 and 2026-07-02 minutes).",
   "expiry_condition_verbatim": null,
   "ordinance_pdf_url": null,
   "_pulled_at": "2026-08-16T16:58:00Z",
   "source_batch": "B",
