  {
   "county": "Dubois",
   "jurisdiction": "Huntingburg (municipal, within Dubois County)",
   "action_type": "proposed",
   "instrument": "Contemplated data center zoning standards, not yet drafted as a formal ordinance: heavy-industrial district plus special-exception requirement; ~500 ft setback from adjacent structures; 55 dB noise threshold; lighting/utility criteria under review",
   "posture_source_words": "Rather than wait and react, let's get ahead of this a little bit... any company seeking to build a data center would need to apply for a special use exception through the Board of Zoning Appeals... that arrangement is not a sustainable long-term solution.",
   "observed_date": "2026-07-30",
   "date_note": "Two dated articles: 2026-07-15 (City Attorney calls current BZA special-exception process unsustainable; mayor to take up the matter after the Aug 24, 2026 budget meeting) and 2026-07-30 (Planning Commission discusses specific candidate standards). No ordinance had been formally directed to be drafted as of the July 30 article; City Council expected to receive the matter in roughly 2-3 months.",
   "effective_from": null,
   "effective_to": null,
   "verbatim_snippet": "\"Rather than wait and react, let's get ahead of this a little bit,\" the Planning Director stated to commissioners. A 500-foot setback from the nearest structure on an adjacent property appears frequently in recently drafted ordinances... A noise threshold of 55 decibels is another figure... no formal directive to draft ordinances has been issued yet.",
   "url": "https://duboiscountyfreepress.com/huntingburg-planning-commission-begins-discussion-on-data-center-zoning-regulations/",
   "doc_type": "news article",
   "evidence_grade": "REPORTED_NEEDS_VERIFICATION",
   "why_codified_misses_it": "Huntingburg's current Unified Development Ordinance has no data-center-specific provisions at all (per the City Attorney's own statement); any future standards remain at the pre-draft discussion stage.",
   "expiry_condition_verbatim": null,
   "ordinance_pdf_url": null,
   "_pulled_at": "2026-08-16T00:00:00Z",
   "source_batch": "F",
   "raw_row": "{\"county\": \"Dubois\", \"jurisdiction\": \"Huntingburg (municipal, within Dubois County)\", \"action_type\": \"proposed\", \"instrument\": \"Contemplated data center zoning standards, not yet drafted as a formal ordinance: heavy-industrial district plus special-exception requirement; ~500 ft setback from adjacent structures; 55 dB noise threshold; lighting/utility criteria under review\", \"posture_source_words\": \"Rather than wait and react, let's get ahead of this a little bit... any company seeking to build a data center would need to apply for a special use exception through the Board of Zoning Appeals... that arrangement is not a sustainable long-term solution.\", \"observed_date\": \"2026-07-30\", \"date_note\": \"Two dated articles: 2026-07-15 (City Attorney calls current BZA special-exception process unsustainable; mayor to take up the matter after the Aug 24, 2026 budget meeting) and 2026-07-30 (Planning Commission discusses specific candidate standards). No ordinance had been formally directed to be drafted as of the July 30 article; City Council expected to receive the matter in roughly 2-3 months.\", \"effective_from\": null, \"effective_to\": null, \"verbatim_snippet\": \"\\\"Rather than wait and react, let's get ahead of this a little bit,\\\" the Planning Director stated to commissioners. A 500-foot setback from the nearest structure on an adjacent property appears frequently in recently drafted ordinances... A noise threshold of 55 decibels is another figure... no formal directive to draft ordinances has been issued yet.\", \"url\": \"https://duboiscountyfreepress.com/huntingburg-planning-commission-begins-discussion-on-data-center-zoning-regulations/\", \"doc_type\": \"news article\", \"evidence_grade\": \"REPORTED_NEEDS_VERIFICATION\", \"why_codified_misses_it\": \"Huntingburg's current Unified Development Ordinance has no data-center-specific provisions at all (per the City Attorney's own statement); any future standards remain at the pre-draft discussion stage.\", \"pulled_at\": \"2026-08-16T00:00:00Z\"}"
