   "effective_from": "2026-02-25",
   "effective_to": null,
   "verbatim_snippet": "Following a 5.5 hour Jefferson County Board of Zoning public hearing Wednesday, the commissioners voted to uphold the decision that a data center can be built at Jefferson Proving Grounds. ... In February, Jefferson County Zoning Administrator Josh Cline determined that the heavy industrial zoning classification of the area did apply to a data center, even though a data center is not specifically listed in the ordinance. Deborah Jones, a Jefferson County resident, appealed that decision. Which the commissioners voted to uphold, instead.",
